[{"slug": "montana-property-tax-guide", "title": "Montana Property Tax Guide: Appeals, Exemptions and Selling With Tax Due", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Montana Property Tax Guide: Appeals, Exemptions and Selling With Tax Due</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Montana</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Montana Property Tax Guide: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Montana Property Tax Guide sale</li><li>Turn the Montana Property Tax Guide offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Montana House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Montana property tax is assessed and collected at the local level, and owners can appeal an assessment.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Owners disagreeing with a valuation must submit Form AB-26 (informal review) within 30 days of the date on the classification and appraisal notice. (Informal Review and Formal Appeal Process (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/appraisal/appeals-and-reviews' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Owners may instead appeal directly to the county tax appeal board by submitting the appeal to the county clerk and recorder within 30 days of the notice date. (Informal Review and Formal Appeal Process (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/appraisal/appeals-and-reviews' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>After a missed 30-day deadline, informal review requests are accepted until June 1, 2026, and adjustments then apply to tax year 2026 only. (Informal Review and Formal Appeal Process (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/appraisal/appeals-and-reviews' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The county tax appeal board (CTAB) is independent of the Department of Revenue and appointed by the county commissioners. (Informal Review and Formal Appeal Process (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/appraisal/appeals-and-reviews' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Decisions of the Montana Tax Appeal Board are final unless the taxpayer pursues district court action. (Informal Review and Formal Appeal Process (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/appraisal/appeals-and-reviews' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Under 15-1-402 MCA, a valid property tax protest requires a written protest filed with the county treasurer and payment of the disputed taxes by the due date. (Informal Review and Formal Appeal Process (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/appraisal/appeals-and-reviews' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Between May 1 and May 30 of the year the redemption period expires, the county treasurer or lien assignee must give notice that a tax deed may issue unless the lien is redeemed. (15-18-212 MCA; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0150/chapter_0180/part_0020/section_0120/0150-0180-0020-0120.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Notice is by certified mail, return receipt requested, to the current occupant and each party on a litigation guarantee. (15-18-212 MCA; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0150/chapter_0180/part_0020/section_0120/0150-0180-0020-0120.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Montana?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Montana houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-homestead-exemption/'>Montana Homestead Exemption Guide</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-estate-tax/'>Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/'>We buy houses in Montana</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Department of Revenue</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Code Annotated</a></li><li><a href='https://courts.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Courts</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Montana Property Tax Guide, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Montana\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Montana Property Tax Guide: Appeals\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-property-tax-guide/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Montana Property Tax Guide: Appeals", "rank_math_description": "Montana property tax: appeals, exemptions, delinquent tax and selling a house with tax due. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "montana property tax"}, {"slug": "montana-homestead-exemption", "title": "Montana Homestead Exemption: Eligibility, Filing and Selling the Home", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Montana Homestead Exemption: Eligibility, Filing and Selling the Home</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Montana</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Montana Homestead Exemption: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Montana Homestead Exemption sale</li><li>Turn the Montana Homestead Exemption offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Montana House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Montana offers property tax relief for qualifying homeowners, and official sources explain the rules.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>The Homestead Reduced Rate lowers property taxes for owners who occupy the Montana home as principal residence at least seven months per year. (Homestead Reduced Tax Rate FAQs (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/property-tax-changes/homestead-faqs' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Eligibility: owner or revocable grantor trust owns the home, owner is current on property taxes, and no other homestead rate is claimed. (Homestead Reduced Tax Rate FAQs (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/property-tax-changes/homestead-faqs' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A Montana homestead declaration (creditor protection, filed with the clerk and recorder) is separate from and does not qualify for the Homestead Reduced Rate. (Homestead Reduced Tax Rate FAQs (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/property-tax-changes/homestead-faqs' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Enrollment for the 2026 tax year closed March 20, 2026; enrollment for 2027 is open. (Homestead Reduced Tax Rate FAQs (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/property-tax-changes/homestead-faqs' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The reduced rate stays with a property through the end of the calendar year after a sale; the buyer must enroll to continue it the next year. (Homestead Reduced Tax Rate FAQs (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/property-tax-changes/homestead-faqs' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A home not previously enrolled is taxed at a flat 1.9% for 2026 for buyers who miss the deadline, with a refund of the difference available Jan 1-May 31, 2027. (Homestead Reduced Tax Rate FAQs (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/property/property-tax-changes/homestead-faqs' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Montana?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Montana houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-property-tax-guide/'>Montana Property Tax Guide: Appeals</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-estate-tax/'>Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/'>We buy houses in Montana</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Department of Revenue</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Code Annotated</a></li><li><a href='https://courts.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Courts</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Montana Homestead Exemption, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Montana\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Montana Homestead Exemption Guide\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-homestead-exemption/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Montana Homestead Exemption Guide", "rank_math_description": "Montana homestead exemption: who qualifies, how to apply and what happens when you sell. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "montana homestead exemption"}, {"slug": "montana-estate-tax", "title": "Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax: What Heirs Owe When Selling", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax: What Heirs Owe When Selling</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Montana</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax sale</li><li>Turn the Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Montana House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>This guide covers what official sources say about Montana estate and inheritance tax.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Montana no longer collects estate or inheritance taxes. (Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/taxes/fiduciaries/estate-and-inheritance-tax' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Montana&#x27;s inheritance tax was repealed in November 2000 and does not apply to deaths after January 1, 2001. (Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/taxes/fiduciaries/estate-and-inheritance-tax' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Montana has no estate tax for deaths after 2004. (Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/taxes/fiduciaries/estate-and-inheritance-tax' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Estate fiduciaries may need to file Form FID-3 (Montana income tax return for estates and trusts) if federal Form 1041 was filed and the decedent owned Montana property or had Montana-source income. (Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/taxes/fiduciaries/estate-and-inheritance-tax' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Montana no longer requires a certificate or consent from the department to close probate or transfer securities. (Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/taxes/fiduciaries/estate-and-inheritance-tax' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Montana?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Montana houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-property-tax-guide/'>Montana Property Tax Guide: Appeals</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-homestead-exemption/'>Montana Homestead Exemption Guide</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/'>We buy houses in Montana</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Department of Revenue</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Code Annotated</a></li><li><a href='https://courts.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Courts</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Montana\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-estate-tax/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax", "rank_math_description": "Montana estate and inheritance tax rules and how they affect heirs selling an inherited house. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "montana estate tax"}, {"slug": "montana-quitclaim-deed", "title": "Montana Quitclaim Deed: Recording, Fees and When It Works", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Montana Quitclaim Deed: Recording, Fees and When It Works</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Montana</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Montana Quitclaim Deed: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Montana Quitclaim Deed sale</li><li>Turn the Montana Quitclaim Deed offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Montana House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>A Montana deed is recorded with the county office named in the sources below.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Use of the word &#x27;grant&#x27; in a conveyance implies only that the grantor has not previously conveyed the estate and that it is free from encumbrances made by the grantor or those claiming under the grantor. (70-20-304 MCA; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0700/chapter_0200/part_0030/section_0040/0700-0200-0030-0040.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A deed transferring real property requires a Realty Transfer Certificate for recording, with exceptions for gifts and transfers between spouses or parent and child for nominal consideration. (15-7-305, 15-7-307 MCA; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0150/chapter_0070/part_0030/section_0070/0150-0070-0030-0070.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Standard document recording fee is $20 for the first page and $10 for each additional page. (7-4-2637 MCA; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0070/chapter_0040/part_0260/section_0370/0070-0040-0260-0370.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A document not meeting 7-4-2636 standards costs the standard fee plus $10. (7-4-2637 MCA; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0070/chapter_0040/part_0260/section_0370/0070-0040-0260-0370.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Beginning July 1, 2027, the Department of Revenue will adjust the recording fee biennially for inflation by rule. (7-4-2637 MCA; <a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0070/chapter_0040/part_0260/section_0370/0070-0040-0260-0370.html' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Montana?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Montana houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-property-tax-guide/'>Montana Property Tax Guide: Appeals</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-homestead-exemption/'>Montana Homestead Exemption Guide</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-estate-tax/'>Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/'>We buy houses in Montana</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Department of Revenue</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Code Annotated</a></li><li><a href='https://courts.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Courts</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Montana Quitclaim Deed, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Montana\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Montana Quitclaim Deed: Recording and Fees\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-quitclaim-deed/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Montana Quitclaim Deed: Recording and Fees", "rank_math_description": "Montana quitclaim deed: how it works, recording and transfer tax rules. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "montana quitclaim deed"}, {"slug": "montana-capital-gains-tax", "title": "Montana Capital Gains Tax When You Sell a House", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Montana Capital Gains Tax When You Sell a House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Montana</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Montana Capital Gains Tax When You Sell a House: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Montana Capital Gains Tax When You Sell a House sale</li><li>Turn the Montana Capital Gains Tax When You Sell a House offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Montana House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>This guide covers what official sources say about Montana tax on a house sale.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Montana taxes long-term capital gains at 3.0% and 4.1%; these rates remain for tax years 2026-2027, with brackets adjusted to match ordinary income. (HB337: 2026-2027 Montana Individual Income Tax Changes (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/news/recent-news/HB-337' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Tax year 2026 ordinary income rates are 4.7% and 5.65%; tax year 2027 rates are 4.7% and 5.4% (taxable income excludes long-term capital gains). (HB337 (MT DOR); <a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/news/recent-news/HB-337' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Montana?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Montana houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-property-tax-guide/'>Montana Property Tax Guide: Appeals</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-homestead-exemption/'>Montana Homestead Exemption Guide</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-estate-tax/'>Montana Estate and Inheritance Tax</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/'>We buy houses in Montana</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://revenue.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Department of Revenue</a></li><li><a href='https://mca.legmt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Code Annotated</a></li><li><a href='https://courts.mt.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Montana Courts</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Montana Capital Gains Tax When You Sell a House, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Montana\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-montana/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Montana Capital Gains Tax on a House Sale\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/montana-capital-gains-tax/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Montana Capital Gains Tax on a House Sale", "rank_math_description": "Montana income tax treatment when you sell a house: what we could confirm on official pages.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "montana capital gains tax"}]